&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MNIST internals series.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://sankethbk.github.io/blog/posts/ml/labs/2026-10-19-lab-1-mnist-from-pixels-to-neural-network/"&gt;Lab 1.1&lt;/a&gt; gave us class templates. &lt;a href="https://sankethbk.github.io/blog/posts/ml/labs/2026-10-19-lab-2-continual-learning-1-2-then-3/"&gt;Lab 1.2&lt;/a&gt; watched them reorganize. &lt;a href="https://sankethbk.github.io/blog/posts/ml/labs/2026-10-27-lab-3-from-templates-to-features/"&gt;Lab 1.3&lt;/a&gt; added a hidden layer and the templates dissolved into shared, position-anchored stroke fragments.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>